WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.773
Kathleen had turned completely white and still.

2
00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:10.811
Gerald was so shocked, he could not speak.

3
00:00:10.812 --> 00:00:14.272
His sister was now made of marble.

4
00:00:14.273 --> 00:00:17.103
At last he called down to Jimmy.

5
00:00:17.104 --> 00:00:20.125
"Kathleen made the ring a wishing ring again.

6
00:00:20.126 --> 00:00:23.684
Then she wished she was a statue."

7
00:00:23.685 --> 00:00:27.212
"And is she?" asked Jimmy.

8
00:00:27.213 --> 00:00:29.135
"Come up and look."

9
00:00:29.136 --> 00:00:31.876
Jimmy climbed into the dinosaur.

10
00:00:31.877 --> 00:00:35.598
"She's really a statue," he said.

11
00:00:35.599 --> 00:00:40.323
"Let's go tell Mabel."

12
00:00:40.324 --> 00:00:43.137
Mabel was still hiding in the bushes.

13
00:00:43.138 --> 00:00:45.858
The boys told her about Kathleen.

14
00:00:45.859 --> 00:00:51.658
Mabel gasped. "What will happen next?"

15
00:00:51.659 --> 00:00:55.544
"She'll go back to normal," said Gerald.

16
00:00:55.545 --> 00:00:59.366
"But what about me?" said Mabel.

17
00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:02.931
"You don't know how frightening it is to be out here like this.

18
00:01:02.932 --> 00:01:05.708
Can't you get the ring?"

19
00:01:05.709 --> 00:01:10.689
"It may have turned to stone, but I'll try," said Gerald.

20
00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:16.088
Gerald climbed back into the dinosaur.

21
00:01:16.089 --> 00:01:18.955
The ring had not turned to marble.

22
00:01:18.956 --> 00:01:24.128
"I'm sorry, Kathleen." He took the ring.

23
00:01:24.129 --> 00:01:26.784
Then he gave it to Mabel.

24
00:01:26.785 --> 00:01:29.511
"Now you won't be afraid of anything."

25
00:01:29.512 --> 00:01:34.482
Mabel wanted to be closer to the dinosaur.

26
00:01:34.483 --> 00:01:39.167
Then she would be near Kathleen when her spell broke.

27
00:01:39.168 --> 00:01:44.745
After she crawled over to the dinosaur, she stood up and looked inside.

28
00:01:44.746 --> 00:01:48.559
"It'll be all right," she reassured Kathleen.

29
00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:53.702
"I'm nearby. Call me when you feel yourself getting better."

30
00:01:53.703 --> 00:01:57.749
Inside her marble shell, Kathleen heard Mabel.

31
00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:02.618
But she couldn't speak.

32
00:02:02.619 --> 00:02:07.762
The boys covered Mabel with the Ugly-Wuglies' clothes so she'd stay warm.

33
00:02:07.763 --> 00:02:15.489
They promised to return later to check on the girls.

34
00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:19.246
Then they went back to the school.

35
00:02:19.247 --> 00:02:24.361
They told Mademoiselle that Kathleen was staying overnight with Mabel.

36
00:02:24.362 --> 00:02:30.811
The sun set and the moon rose.

37
00:02:30.812 --> 00:02:33.697
Mabel fell asleep.

38
00:02:33.698 --> 00:02:39.952
Inside the dinosaur Kathleen knew she must wait patiently for her own spell to break.

39
00:02:39.953 --> 00:02:46.221
Soon she fell asleep.

40
00:02:46.222 --> 00:02:50.209
Kathleen woke up suddenly in the middle of the night.

41
00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:53.137
The dinosaur was moving!

42
00:02:53.138 --> 00:02:56.702
"Oh, how dreadful!" she said.

43
00:02:56.703 --> 00:03:00.045
"The dinosaur must have come alive in the moonlight.

44
00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:04.173
That's what Gerald said happened to the statues."

45
00:03:04.174 --> 00:03:08.936
She was afraid to drop through the hole while the statue moved.

46
00:03:08.937 --> 00:03:10.662
But where was Mabel?

47
00:03:10.663 --> 00:03:13.832
What if the dinosaur stepped on her?

48
00:03:13.833 --> 00:03:16.242
Kathleen peered through the hole.

49
00:03:16.243 --> 00:03:19.329
The dinosaur was moving faster.

50
00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:22.515
The floor of its stomach sloped downward.

51
00:03:22.516 --> 00:03:25.647
They were going downhill.

52
00:03:25.648 --> 00:03:30.243
Through the hole Kathleen saw grass and then stone.

53
00:03:30.244 --> 00:03:32.465
She heard the splash of water.

54
00:03:32.466 --> 00:03:34.688
They were near the lake.

55
00:03:34.689 --> 00:03:37.572
The dinosaur was about to go swimming!

56
00:03:37.573 --> 00:03:43.054
Kathleen jumped through the hole just as the dinosaur reached the lake.

57
00:03:43.055 --> 00:03:51.842
She raced into the Temple of Apollo.

58
00:03:51.843 --> 00:03:58.798
"Be still, little lady," said a voice. "I leap."

59
00:03:58.799 --> 00:04:04.570
Kathleen watched as the statue of Apollo leaped from the pedestal.

60
00:04:04.571 --> 00:04:08.602
"You're new here," said Apollo.

61
00:04:08.603 --> 00:04:12.429
"I'm quite new," said Kathleen.

62
00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:16.097
"I didn't know you could talk."

63
00:04:16.098 --> 00:04:18.987
"Why not? You can."

64
00:04:18.988 --> 00:04:23.027
"But I'm alive," said Kathleen.

65
00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:27.427
"And so am I," said the statue.

66
00:04:27.428 --> 00:04:29.421
"I suppose so.

67
00:04:29.422 --> 00:04:33.441
But I thought I'd need the ring to see you."

68
00:04:33.442 --> 00:04:35.033
"That's for mortals.

69
00:04:35.034 --> 00:04:41.373
We statues can hear and see each other."

70
00:04:41.374 --> 00:04:45.156
At that, Apollo dove into the lake.

71
00:04:45.157 --> 00:04:54.556
Kathleen wanted to get Mabel and go home.

72
00:04:54.557 --> 00:04:59.267
She found Mabel sleeping under the pile of Ugly-Wugly clothing.

73
00:04:59.268 --> 00:05:02.408
"Wake up!" she called.

74
00:05:02.409 --> 00:05:07.541
"I want to go home," said Mabel.

75
00:05:07.542 --> 00:05:11.070
"So do I, but you can't go home like that.

76
00:05:11.071 --> 00:05:13.564
You're still too tall."

77
00:05:13.565 --> 00:05:15.877
Mabel closed her eyes.

78
00:05:15.878 --> 00:05:19.438
"Oh, Kathleen, I feel so funny.

79
00:05:19.439 --> 00:05:21.763
Am I shrinking?"

80
00:05:21.764 --> 00:05:26.864
"Yes!" said Kathleen. "Now we can go home."

81
00:05:26.865 --> 00:05:30.018
"But what about you?"

82
00:05:30.019 --> 00:05:34.688
"What do you mean? I'm fine," said Kathleen.

83
00:05:34.689 --> 00:05:36.854
"Look at yourself."

84
00:05:36.855 --> 00:05:42.251
Kathleen looked down at her hands and her dress.

85
00:05:42.252 --> 00:05:47.206
"Why am I this horrid color?" she cried.

86
00:05:47.207 --> 00:05:51.158
"Don't you understand?" asked Mabel.

87
00:05:51.159 --> 00:06:00.444
"You're still a statue!"

